Remove Supabase entirely, and explain why scans found nothing

SUPABASE IS GONE

Sign-in, sign-up and sign-out now run on this Worker: PBKDF2 through
WebCrypto, sessions as signed HttpOnly cookies, both already covered by
their own suites. The client, the middleware, the generated types, the
session bridge, the old pipeline and photo-url helpers, the package and
every SUPABASE_ variable are deleted.

That was also the cause of the permission confusion. Two identity systems
disagreed about who someone was, which is how an account could create a
collection and then be refused when uploading into it. There is one now,
and the role travels with the session.

The operator credentials in the environment are authoritative: they create
the console account when missing and repair its password when it exists.
Accounts left behind by the bridge hold a deliberately unusable password,
so without that the operator could never sign in to their own console.

WHY A SCAN RETURNED NOTHING

Vectorize applies writes asynchronously. Its info endpoint reports how far
it has processed, and a scan run moments after an upload genuinely cannot
see those faces yet. Telling someone there are no matches is wrong then,
and sends them away for good, so a scan now reports that the index is still
catching up and asks them to try again.

A match whose photo record is missing is also counted rather than silently
dropped: a scan that matches faces and shows nothing needs a completely
different fix from one that matched nothing.

ERRORS NO LONGER SAY NOTHING

Every API error returns JSON with the message and a short reference that is
logged beside the stack, instead of an HTML page that reaches the browser as
a bare 500.

